{
  "id": "medicaid-waiver",
  "term": "Medicaid Waiver",
  "definition": "A Medicaid Waiver, in this context, is a state program under Home and Community Based Services 1915(c) that allows disability services to be funded in community settings rather than only through standard arrangements. Eligibility and individual funding levels are determined by judging a person’s needs and matching support budgets to their service requirements, with states varying in the tools they use.",
