      "reasons": [
        "The claim that Medicaid waivers allow disability services “rather than only through standard arrangements” is not supported in the provided packet text.",
        "The packet supports that 1915(c) HCBS Medicaid waivers let states fund community-delivered disability services, that individual support budgets are allocated based on a determination of client need and alignment to service requirements, and that the method/tools vary by state; however, the definition’s “rather than only through standard arrangements” wording introduces an unsupported contrast."
